        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "de24d235-befd-54ff-8d2f-196b05cb22aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lansing, Michigan; Ingham County; Eaton County; Clinton County; Michigan; Morgantown, West Virginia; Frankfort, Indiana\n- Companies: Lansing State Journal; Dominion News; Dayton Daily News; The Times; Gannett\n- People: Ronald Clair Roat\n- Topics: Newspapers; city population; state capitals\n\nFacts:\n- Lansing is the capital of the U.S. state of Michigan.\n- Lansing is mostly in Ingham County, and parts of the city extend into Eaton County and Clinton County.\n- The 2010 Census recorded Lansing's population as 114,297, making it the fifth-largest city in Michigan.\n- The Lansing State Journal is a daily newspaper published in Lansing, Michigan.\n- Gannett owns the Lansing State Journal.\n- Ronald Clair Roat's newspapers included the Lansing State Journal, Dominion News of Morgantown, West Virginia, Dayton Daily News, and The Times in Frankfort, Indiana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
